<p>(a)In the third quarter of 1996, L-P recorded a charge of $350 million ($215 million after income taxes, or $2.00 per share) related to the closure of a subsidiary's pulp mill in Ketchikan, Alaska, the settlement of all outstanding shareholder securities class action claims, a reserve for other litigation and a reserve for the planned shutdown and other costs related to certain other non-strategic facilities.</p>
<p>(aa)In the first quarter of 1997, L-P's Ketchikan Pulp Company subsidiary recorded a net gain of $122 million ($74 million after income taxes, or $.68 per share) to reflect the initial amount paid under a settlement agreement with the U.S. Government over claims related to the long-term timber spply contract in Alaska, net of adjustments to closure-related accruals.</p>
